      "content": "thanks for the summary. but i'm a bit confused by how you're characterizing the \"nuanced reality.\" \n\nyou mention that the exodus was \"accelerated\" by the military collapse and chaos, but you also say it wasn't a \"single systematic expulsion policy.\" if there were widespread instances of violence and \"strategic decisions\" made by the military to clear areas, wouldn't most historians argue that's essentially a systematic policy of expulsion by another name? \n\ni'm trying to figure out if there's a legitimate scholarly distinction between \"chaos and fear\" and \"a systematic policy,\" or if scientists/historians generally view that distinction as a way to avoid using the word \"expulsion.\" how should i frame this distinction in my paper so i don't look like i'm just avoiding the harsher reality?",
